# Subagent: SOTA Model Retrainer (Encoder Fix Verification)

## Task
Re-run the full SOTA training pipeline using the fixed encoder weight transfer code.
The previous run failed to transfer pre-trained encoder weights into fine-tuning.
This run verifies the fix works end-to-end.

## Context
- You are in /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine
- PYTHONPATH=/Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine
- Training script: scripts/train_sota.py
- Harvested data: trained_data/harvest/*.parquet (15 pairs)
- Previous pretrain weights are INVALID (saved with wrong namespace) — they will be overwritten

## Exact Commands
1. Delete old invalid pretrain weights:
   rm -f trained_data/models/sota_pretrain/pretrain_weights.weights.h5

2. Run Phase 1 pre-training:
   cd /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine
   PYTHONPATH=/Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine python scripts/train_sota.py --pretrain-only

3. Verify pretrain weights exist:
   ls -lh trained_data/models/sota_pretrain/pretrain_weights.weights.h5

4. Run Phase 2 fine-tuning:
   PYTHONPATH=/Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine python scripts/train_sota.py --finetune-only

5. Check final model:
   ls -lh trained_data/models/sota_finetuned/sota_model.keras

## Expected Behavior
- Phase 1: val_loss should decrease monotonically
- Phase 2: direction accuracy should be BETTER than ~50% (previous coin-flip result)
- If encoder transfer works, accuracy should climb above 55% within first few epochs
- No Keras 3 crashes (class_weight already removed, skip_mismatch no longer needed)

## If Training Crashes
- Report the error with traceback
- Do NOT modify source code unless it's a trivial obvious bug
- If it's a bug you can fix quickly (one-liner), fix it and continue

## Report Format
Save your report to /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine/tmp/subagents/sota_retrain_report.md with:
- Phase 1 results (epochs, best val_loss)
- Phase 2 results (epochs, final accuracy, direction_loss)
